		"exercise_5_9_angle_between": {
			"name": "Angle Between Vectors",
			"lookup_name": "exercise_5_9_angle_between",
			"description": "Two thin arrows rise from a common centre in the XY plane with a pink figure drawn between them and a live degree readout above; two 3D sliders turn each arrow independently. DNA axes: opening (agreeing / strangers / opposing / parallel - the case the pair is found in, the same word and the same four values as the sibling agreement_gauge) and figure (arc / wedge / chord / none - what the angle is drawn as, where chord is the difference vector steering code actually computes).",
			"scene": "res://algorithms/steering/noc_ch05/exercise_5_9_angle_between_vr.tscn",
			"category": "steering",
			"dna": {
				"promoted": "2026-08-03",
				"stage": "2 - variation",
				"axes": {
					"opening": [
						"agreeing",
						"strangers",
						"opposing",
						"parallel"
					],
					"figure": [
						"arc",
						"wedge",
						"chord",
						"none"
					]
				},
				"default": "opening=agreeing, figure=arc - _opening_angle() returns the shipped literal PI / 3.0 for agreeing (angle_a stays 0.0), and the arc branch is the shipped _update_arc(center, 0.12, angle_a, angle_b) call reached through the match default, so the 3 existing placements draw the same 60-degree pair and the same 20-segment line strip they always did. The wedge and chord meshes are only ever built when a map asks for them",
				"was": "two float @exports (angle_a, angle_b) with no enum shape, an apply_grid_config() whose body was `pass`, and one welded figure: a 20-segment arc of radius 0.12 was the only thing 'the angle between' could look like. The stage-2 sweep read no turnable knob. Every placement opened on the same acute pair, and the three cases the exercise exists to teach - perpendicular, obtuse, coincident - were reachable only by a player dragging a slider",
				"shared_with": "agreement_gauge - `opening` is that artifact's word with that artifact's four values in the same order, because it is literally the same question asked of the same pair of directions. A room can now set the gauge and the exercise to the same case and the two will mean the same thing by it; if the vocabulary is honest they should MEASURE alike",
				"note": "hand promotion 2026-08-03 - the runner refused it for NO TURNABLE KNOBS. opening turns theta alone: agreeing 60 deg (shipped), strangers 90 (dot exactly zero), opposing 120 (dot negative), parallel 0 (the arrows superimpose, the figure collapses to a point and the readout still answers). figure is the axis that puts the exercise's own title at risk - arc says the angle is a rotation, wedge says it is an area, none says it is only a digit, and chord draws the tip-to-tip segment, which IS the difference vector; no steering routine ever takes an arc, so chord is the reading the chapter actually uses in code. Under chord the readout gains a |b - a| line so a still cannot misreport which claim is on screen. The two angle sliders stay live under every value: opening sets the case the exercise is found in, it does not lock it",
				"gotcha": "the angle sliders round to step_size 0.01, so the shipped PI / 3.0 has always been stored as 1.05 after ParameterController3D.set_value re-emits. The promotion routes opening through the same set_value path, so it inherits that rounding rather than introducing a second convention"
			},
